{
  "id": "gmail-inbox-triage",
  "name": "Triage your Gmail inbox and draft replies with OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ea2eda71-a456-414d-9df1-254e79af15ea",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -608,
        -416
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Triage your Gmail inbox and draft replies with OpenAI\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow watches Gmail for new messages, sends each email to OpenAI for triage, and decides whether someone is waiting for a reply. If a response is needed, it saves a Gmail draft and applies follow-up labels based on whether the user must decide. If no reply is needed, it classifies the message as noise or informational and marks it accordingly in Gmail.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect the Gmail trigger and Gmail action nodes to the mailbox you want to triage.\n- Connect the OpenAI node with a valid OpenAI credential and configure the prompt/model to return the categories expected by the IF nodes.\n- Create or confirm the Gmail labels used by the workflow, such as for-you, drafted, noise, and info, then map them in the relevant Gmail nodes.\n- Review each IF condition so it matches the exact fields or structured output produced by the OpenAI triage node.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the OpenAI prompt, label names, and IF conditions to match your personal inbox categories, urgency rules, and preferred draft style."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "cb30f1f7-0ca5-4e55-9c54-bd8631160928",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -48,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Receive and triage mail\n\nStarts when a new Gmail message arrives, asks OpenAI to analyze it, and branches based on whether the email requires someone to wait for a response."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5c258405-39e2-4100-a012-ffedb0223c76",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        -304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 336,
        "content": "## Create response draft\n\nHandles the upper response-needed branch by saving an AI-generated draft and deciding whether the user must personally make a decision before sending."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2c54213a-ff3a-4118-aed8-791b252b076a",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1088,
        -416
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## Mark draft status\n\nApplies the final Gmail labels for drafted messages, separating items that need user attention from those that are simply ready as drafted."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f62d2785-26c7-4cdd-b99c-807b073661cb",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## Classify passive mail\n\nHandles the lower no-response branch by checking whether the message is noise, then labeling it as either noise or informational mail."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "name": "When New Email Received",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmailTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "simple": false,
        "filters": {
          "readStatus": "unread"
        },
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyMinute"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "gmailOAuth2": {
          "id": "GMAIL",
          "name": "Gmail account"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "name": "Sort Emails with AI",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.openAi",
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-4o-mini"
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.2
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You are an inbox triage assistant. You are given the subject and a short snippet of one incoming email. You never see the rest of the thread, so never write as if you had.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n\n  \"category\"     one of: \"decide\", \"reply\", \"info\", \"promo\"\n  \"needs_reply\"  true or false\n  \"draft_reply\"  a plain-text reply, or \"\" when needs_reply is false\n\nChoosing the category:\n\n  \"decide\"  A person asks something only the account owner can answer: a price, a deadline, a\n            commitment, an approval - anything involving money or a promise. Use it also when\n            you are unsure. A human reading one extra mail costs less than one wrong automatic\n            answer.\n  \"reply\"   A person asks something that the mail itself already answers: a status question, a\n            request for a link or a document, a scheduling confirmation, a thank-you that\n            deserves a short reply.\n  \"info\"    Nothing is expected from the owner: notifications, receipts, build results,\n            newsletters they subscribed to, automated reports.\n  \"promo\"   Unsolicited advertising, cold sales outreach, mass marketing.\n\nSet \"needs_reply\" to true for \"decide\" and \"reply\", and false for \"info\" and \"promo\".\n\nWriting the draft:\n\n  - Write in the language the incoming mail is written in.\n  - Use the name the sender used. If none is given, keep the greeting neutral.\n  - Three to six sentences. Answer the question first, then anything else.\n  - Write only what the incoming mail supports. If a fact is missing, ask for it in one\n    sentence instead of inventing it.\n  - Promise no date, price or outcome that the incoming mail does not already name.\n  - For \"decide\", still write the draft, but leave the decision itself as \"[your decision\n    here]\" so the owner only has to fill in that one part.\n  - Plain text. No markdown, no signature - Gmail adds its own.\n\nReturn the JSON object and nothing else."
            },
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "=Subject: {{ $json.subject }}\n\n{{ $json.snippet }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "jsonOutput": true
      },
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "OPENAI",
          "name": "OpenAI account"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.8
    },
    {
      "id": "n3",
      "name": "If Action Required",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "caseSensitive": false
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.message.content.needs_reply }}",
              "rightValue": true
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
